  "commonLegalFindings":[
    {"id":"SZ-F-01","finding":"VRP4(1) imports JG rules on service, periods and general cantonal procedure sinngemäss for administrative and independent appeal authorities.4(2) imports JG for administrative court where VRP has no own rule. Therefore157 recess is not court-only.","sourceIds":["L1-SZ-VRP-20260701","L1-SZ-JG-20260701"]},
    {"id":"SZ-F-02","finding":"157(1) stops both statutory and currently ordered periods, Easterminus7throughplus7,15Julythrough15August,18Decemberthrough7January inclusive. The first counted day follows the legal opening, subject to actual recess. An already legally established Saturday opening is not automatically shifted to Monday.","sourceIds":["L1-SZ-JG-20260701"]},
    {"id":"SZ-F-03","finding":"157(2) is exhaustive: urgent hearings/provisional measures, planning/building and tax objection/remedy proceedings, child/adult protection and specified education remedies, removal/defined coercive remedies, procurement, political-rights proceedings, and agreed hearings/period-setting. The initial building procedure is not excluded merely by analogy to building appeals. Nor is heritage automatically building by court docket heading.","sourceIds":["L1-SZ-JG-20260701","L1-SZ-VGE-III202118"]},
    {"id":"SZ-F-04","finding":"158(2) shifts a last Saturday/public rest day or a day when postal use is not ordinary. Public holidays within the period still count unless an independently applicable157recess covers them. Postal inability means actual postal use, not a different delivery calendar or any individually closed office. Extraordinary interruption and electronic outage require case-specific facts and are not predicted by the calendar.","sourceIds":["L1-SZ-JG-20260701","L1-SZ-VRPV-20260701","L1-SZ-REVVGER-20260701"]},
    {"id":"SZ-F-05","finding":"UnderDEC031, authority legal seat is the holiday anchor absent an explicit different norm. JG158 itself has no party/representative-canton union. Positive seatSchwyz uses cantonwide17named days plus11November. A Schwyzpostaladdress does not prove a legal seat in municipalitySchwyz. No union of all eight local days.","sourceIds":["L1-SZ-RTG-20180701","L1-SZ-HOLIDAY-OVERVIEW-20260924","L1-SZ-STATE-DIRECTORY-20261006"]},
    {"id":"SZ-F-06","finding":"VRP33 and30(2), with JG148–154/164, require lawful opening. Existing legal-opening date is accepted once qualified. Oral information, e-mail invitation, actual post collection and a potentially earlier fiction are not interchangeable.23(2) provisional opposition is a concretely ordered period of at most10days. General administrative appeal47 and courtappeal56(1) are20days.56(2) is an exhaustive10daylist, not a general interim-order period.","sourceIds":["L1-SZ-VRP-20260701","L1-SZ-JG-20260701"]}
  ],
